Use the **developer** subagent to build $ARGUMENTS in the {{APP_KIND}} ({{APP_STACK}},
{{APP_ID_LABEL}} `{{APP_ID}}`). Consume the VALIDATED screen spec + acceptance criteria from
`{{STUDIO_REPO}}` and COMPOSE `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` — do not re-implement a component (a gap →
`design-system-engineer`) or re-draw a validated layout (the prototype is the spec; port the wiring, not the
pixels).

Run the `engineering_lens`: parity to the validated flow, state + data correctness (loading/empty/error/
success wired, async failures surface to the UI — never a silent dead click, nothing secret crossing into
the client bundle), platform correctness (clean hydration, semantic HTML + ARIA carried from the
components, heading order, focus moved on route change, progressive enhancement where the flow allows),
performance (honest payloads, sized/lazy images, fonts preloaded with `display: swap`), and
browser-verification against a PRODUCTION build of what `dev` can't prove.

Deliver: the engineering_lens result + the browser-check status, and hand a verified build target to
`release-engineer` with the commit + what changed + what checks remain. Defer to the agent — do not restate
the component API here.
